CommitDate: Mon Aug 31 14:14:10 2026 -0400

    feat(display): per-conversation display overrides via display.chats
    
    Adds `display.chats.<chat-id>.<key>`, resolved ahead of the per-platform and
    global settings, so a single conversation can be quietened without changing the
    rest of that platform. The motivating case is a shared family group that should
    not see tool-progress bubbles, interim commentary or thinking output, while
    direct messages keep them.
    
    Resolution order becomes: chat -> platform -> global -> platform default ->
    global default.
    
    Tests cover the new precedence and the progress paths that consume it; docs
    gain a worked example under the display section.

